---
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="First Known Use — Portfolio">
  <article class="project">
    <header class="project__header">
      <p class="eyebrow">Project / music identity and web experience</p>
      <h1>First Known Use</h1>
      <p class="project__summary">
        An identity and web experience for a Burlington, Vermont music project creating work that feels both
        familiar and experimental.
      </p>
      <p><a href="https://firstknownuse.com/" rel="external">Visit the project ↗</a></p>
    </header>

    <figure class="project__image" transition:name="first-known-use-window" transition:animate="none">
      <img
        src="/assets/first-known-use/fishwallpaper.png"
        alt="A small black pixel fish and handwritten fish mark on a dark green field."
        width="1920"
        height="1080"
      />
      <figcaption>A visual fragment from the First Known Use project.</figcaption>
    </figure>

    <div class="project__context">
      <p>
        First Known Use extends music into releases, lyrics, images, and a playful digital world. This portfolio
        entry is a context layer around the finished project, with an experimental fragment kept separate from
        the portfolio shell.
      </p>
    </div>

    <section class="case-study" aria-labelledby="case-study-title">
      <div class="case-study__intro">
        <p class="eyebrow">Case study</p>
        <h2 id="case-study-title">A band site built to feel like an artifact.</h2>
        <p>
          The brief called for something between a photocopied poster, a music archive, and a small digital world.
          The result treats releases, lyrics, photographs, and contact information as parts of one living identity
          rather than separate content silos.
        </p>
      </div>

      <dl class="case-study__details">
        <div>
          <dt>Contribution</dt>
          <dd>Design direction, development, and technical architecture</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Built with</dt>
          <dd>Astro, TypeScript, TinaCMS, and Cloudflare</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Content</dt>
          <dd>Releases, lyrics, gallery, bio, and contact</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Editorial need</dt>
          <dd>A band-friendly editing workflow without flattening the visual language</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </section>

    <section class="process" aria-labelledby="process-title">
      <p class="eyebrow">How it came together</p>
      <h2 id="process-title">The identity leads; the system stays out of the way.</h2>
      <ol class="process__list">
        <li>
          <h3>Translate the reference</h3>
          <p>
            Dense type, monochrome imagery, fluorescent accents, doodles, and timetable-like structures became a
            vocabulary for the site instead of a rigid component library.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Make the archive usable</h3>
          <p>
            Releases connect to tracks, lyrics, listening links, and visual material while remaining authored by the
            people who make the music.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Leave room for play</h3>
          <p>
            Marquees, hover treatments, small easter eggs, and alternate themes add movement and surprise without
            making the essential content depend on JavaScript.
          </p>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </section>

  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .project { max-width: 90rem; min-width: 0; margin-inline: auto; padding-top: clamp(3rem, 10vw, 8rem); }
  .project__header { max-width: 62rem; }
  .eyebrow { font-size: 0.8rem; letter-spacing: 0.12em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  h1 { margin-block: 1rem; font-size: clamp(4rem, 16vw, 14rem); line-height: 0.8; letter-spacing: -0.06em; }
  .project__summary { max-width: 40rem; font-size: clamp(1.25rem, 3vw, 2rem); }
  .project__image {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 70rem;
    margin: clamp(3rem, 8vw, 7rem) auto 0;
    overflow: hidden;
    border: 1px solid var(--earthsong-muted);
  }
  .project__image img { display: block; width: 100%; max-width: 100%; height: auto; }
  .project__image figcaption { margin-top: 0.75rem; color: var(--earthsong-muted); font-size: 0.85rem; }
  .project__context { max-width: 32rem; margin: 5rem 0 0 auto; }
  a { font-weight: 700; }

  .case-study, .process { margin-top: clamp(5rem, 12vw, 10rem); }
  .case-study { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(16rem, 0.7fr); gap: clamp(2rem, 8vw, 8rem); }
  .case-study__intro { max-width: 42rem; }
  .case-study h2, .process h2 { max-width: 15ch; margin-block: 0.75rem 1.5rem; font-size: clamp(2.25rem, 6vw, 5.5rem); line-height: 0.95; }
  .case-study__details { margin: 0; }
  .case-study__details div { border-top: 1px solid currentColor; padding-block: 1rem; }
  .case-study__details div:last-child { border-bottom: 1px solid currentColor; }
  .case-study__details dt { font-size: 0.8rem; letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .case-study__details dd { margin: 0.35rem 0 0; }
  .process__list { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 1px; margin: 0; padding: 0; list-style: none; border-block: 1px solid currentColor; }
  .process__list li { padding: 1.5rem 1rem 1.5rem 0; }
  .process__list li + li { padding-left: 1rem; border-left: 1px solid currentColor; }
  .process__list h3 { margin: 0 0 0.75rem; font-size: 1.2rem; }
  .process__list p { margin: 0; }

  @media (max-width: 42rem) {
    h1 { font-size: clamp(3.5rem, 20vw, 7rem); }
    .project__context { margin-top: 3rem; }
    .case-study { display: block; }
    .case-study__details { margin-top: 3rem; }
    .process__list { display: block; }
    .process__list li + li { padding-left: 0; border-top: 1px solid currentColor; border-left: 0; }
  }
</style>
